# This repository is worked on from Windows (core.autocrlf=true here), but
# every file it ships runs on Linux inside a container. Normalise to LF in
# the repository and on checkout, so a Windows clone cannot produce a CRLF
# file that Linux then refuses.
#
# The concrete failure this prevents: backend/docker-entrypoint.sh with a
# CRLF shebang fails at container start with an opaque
#   exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# because the kernel reads the interpreter as "/bin/sh\r". The Dockerfile
# also seds \r out as a second line of defence; this stops it arising.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a CRLF is fatal rather than untidy.
*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.conf        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
